WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.512
How we'll know it's
working, and what I'd need.

2
00:00:02.512 --> 00:00:05.469
Six measures, each baselined
in the first phase,

3
00:00:05.469 --> 00:00:08.728
and each one a business
measure leadership can read:

4
00:00:08.728 --> 00:00:11.760
time from separation to
blocked access, in hours,

5
00:00:11.760 --> 00:00:16.383
against an agency-approved threshold;
credential and access revocation,

6
00:00:16.383 --> 00:00:18.657
reconciled to verified completion,

7
00:00:18.657 --> 00:00:24.038
where one credential-specific constraint
is the federal requirement to terminate a

8
00:00:24.038 --> 00:00:29.040
PIV card that can't be collected within
eighteen hours; accounts tied to a person,

9
00:00:29.040 --> 00:00:33.922
with orphaned accounts trending to zero;
joiner and mover tickets going down,

10
00:00:33.922 --> 00:00:38.358
with access ready on day one; the
manager and organization in the

11
00:00:38.358 --> 00:00:42.962
directory matching HR; and every
exception with an owner and an age.

12
00:00:42.962 --> 00:00:48.262
As a byproduct, the same data is evidence
for the controls auditors ask about.

13
00:00:48.262 --> 00:00:51.186
I'm asking leadership to
make three decisions:

14
00:00:51.186 --> 00:00:53.648
name identity as an HR 2.0 data consumer,

15
00:00:53.648 --> 00:00:57.110
authorize the cross-functional
data-governance work,

16
00:00:57.110 --> 00:01:02.726
and require assumptions to be validated by
accountable owners before implementation.

17
00:01:02.726 --> 00:01:07.008
That lets the agency modernize the
platforms and the lifecycle together,

18
00:01:07.008 --> 00:01:09.887
rather than carrying the
ticket process forward.

19
00:01:09.887 --> 00:01:10.650
Thank you.

20
00:01:10.650 --> 00:01:12.750
I look forward to your questions.
